#: search2:search2_17E59A1E_C2AD_472F_A3C9_CA533D23C576
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: abe9bb473ff69754031bff7401fa3be80685d5155dc4627a12328e2c8532f42e
#. default-sha256: ac251dfdacc35647324416102f99cb7755655b90950316f464e1800b68b0912e
msgctxt "search2:search2_17E59A1E_C2AD_472F_A3C9_CA533D23C576"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫The words of one foolish woman determined the course of my entire life. ⟪k:2⟫Before I "
"was even born, my fate was decided.⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫Did her claim come from faith? Was it her way "
"of escaping reality? Did she do it for money? Or fame? I don’t know."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Le parole di una sola, sciocca donna decisero il corso della mia intera esistenza. ⟪k:2⟫"
"Il mio destino era già stato scritto ancor prima che io nascessi.⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫La sua "
"dichiarazione veniva dalla fede? Era il suo modo di fuggire dalla realtà? Lo faceva per i soldi? "
"O per la fama? Non ne ho idea."

#: search2:search2_1089FD7A_2480_4B50_930C_A13BD08F918B
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 604f8efb8da41c1b16bac011780fe15d43b97bfe290bea9b78f6c64aa697868d
#. default-sha256: a6828ecc9707a8eb462b92b1d10dfd3837c15f49e2065c0b6c42e6027e866488
msgctxt "search2:search2_1089FD7A_2480_4B50_930C_A13BD08F918B"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫The village where she lived had suffered from years of poor harvest. ⟪k:2⟫It had been "
"months since the last rain, and all the villagers prayed desperately to be blessed with succor."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Il villaggio dove lei abitava aveva sofferto per anni di un raccolto misero. ⟪k:2⟫Erano "
"passati mesi dall’ultima pioggia, e tutti gli abitanti pregavano disperatamente affinché "
"ricevessero un aiuto dall’alto."

#: search2:search2_92D9C1B4_DF69_4220_8D5A_EBEDCA4D3909
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 0f81dce5ee68a0dec0c60a07526c1a09e12d9ff695960248fc39c75505c1b999
#. default-sha256: e6d79865233d66ba01e6189fbfcf7fc628fe38178b4fd4cdbf38d39e26a7756c
msgctxt "search2:search2_92D9C1B4_DF69_4220_8D5A_EBEDCA4D3909"
msgid "⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫⟪k:2⟫“I am with child, though I have known no man!”"
msgstr "⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫⟪k:2⟫“Aspetto un bambino,⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫nonostante non sia stata con nessun uomo!”"

#: search2:search2_D097AA71_4A38_41C0_91E3_5AE8CB17787F
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: dba6a2da8272abb5148d5e0453d21c7238ebb6313a964e25f93ac17bd55fb692
#. default-sha256: ca17e74b8d52db4509c637061a359e6a6821060f577236bc9ab8cff257197b42
msgctxt "search2:search2_D097AA71_4A38_41C0_91E3_5AE8CB17787F"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫So proclaimed the pregnant woman in the midst of the drought.⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫And on the "
"day of my birth, the very moment I let out my first cry,⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫a heavy rain fell down upon the "
"village.⟪k:7⟫⟪k:8⟫⟪k:9⟫The storm quenched the parched earth, nourishing the crops and saving the "
"village. ⟪k:10⟫The villagers were astounded, for they had thought the drought would never end."
"⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫⟪k:13⟫As plump drops of rain poured down upon the village, they gathered around "
"newborn me in exultation."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Così proclamò la donna incinta, durante la siccità.⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫E il giorno della mia "
"nascita, nel momento stesso in cui emisi il mio primo vagito,⟪k:5⟫ sul villaggio scese una forte "
"pioggia.⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫⟪k:8⟫Il temporale assetò la terra inaridita, nutrendo i campi e salvando il "
"villaggio. ⟪k:9⟫I paesani rimasero sconvolti, poiché pensavano che la siccità non sarebbe mai "
"giunta a una fine.⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫Mentre gonfie gocce di pioggia si riversavano sul villaggio, "
"i suoi abitanti si riunirono attorno alla neonata esultando."

#: search2:search2_97488FB8_DEDE_4B47_9455_21D6335BF989
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 6eda361b40f118c402c60889bacde8970f1eb89c85c56b869caa49452f45bded
#. default-sha256: 433f786be90a779f53e878d6b8bb6d895c0bb1e4c60b22ac08641fd18bcf9c57
msgctxt "search2:search2_97488FB8_DEDE_4B47_9455_21D6335BF989"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Perhaps there would be more wonder in claiming I had magical powers. ⟪k:2⟫Perhaps it "
"would make a better story if I were to say there were higher forces involved. ⟪k:3⟫But all these "
"years later, here is what I truly think:⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫It was nothing more than a fluke. "
"⟪k:8⟫An improbable stroke of luck.⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫An unbelievably fortunate accident for my mother and "
"the village—⟪k:11⟫and an indescribably unfortunate accident for myself."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Forse ci sarebbe più meraviglia nel sostenere che avessi poteri magici. ⟪k:2⟫Forse ne "
"uscirebbe una storia migliore se dicessi che erano coinvolte forze superiori. ⟪k:3⟫Ma dopo tutti "
"questi anni, ecco cosa penso veramente:⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫Non era stata altro che una "
"coincidenza. ⟪k:8⟫Un improbabile colpo di fortuna.⟪k:9⟫ Un incidente incredibilmente fortunato "
"per mia madre e il villaggio—⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫e un incidente indescrivibilmente disgraziato per me "
"stessa."

#: search2:search2_C8331C9D_43DB_4A92_B3F6_F0917106E78F
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: a47159504cbebbf13342d0fffaa1f8ef74068102d05a9c5dfc3bccc9c24147e8
#. default-sha256: 328d8eab286e3e406521750c990401aea16dac97d8d5aab36db4c211d0c27267
msgctxt "search2:search2_C8331C9D_43DB_4A92_B3F6_F0917106E78F"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Michel... the time when I lived and the time when you lived were not so different. ⟪k:2⟫"
"Our views and beliefs about the world are very much the same, ⟪k:3⟫so you should understand that "
"in our time, blood was seen as unclean. ⟪k:4⟫It was a dreadful thing, ridden with diseases, which "
"is why we drained the blood from animals and purified the flesh before consuming it.⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫"
"⟪k:7⟫But being a saint, my blood would have been different. ⟪k:8⟫Like the blood of the saints who "
"came before me, mine would be blessed.⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫I believed it would be able to cleanse people’s "
"impurities."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Michel... le epoche in cui io e te abbiamo vissuto non erano tanto diverse tra loro. "
"⟪k:2⟫Le nostre opinioni e convinzioni riguardo al mondo erano più o meno le stesse, ⟪k:3⟫quindi "
"dovresti sapere che nel nostro tempo, il sangue veniva visto come qualcosa di impuro. ⟪k:4⟫Era "
"qualcosa di orribile, colmo di malattie, per questo tiravamo fuori il sangue dagli animali e ne "
"purificavamo la carne prima di consumarla.⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫Ma essendo una santa, il mio sangue "
"sarebbe stato diverso. ⟪k:8⟫Come il sangue delle sante venute prima di me, il mio sarebbe stato "
"benedetto.⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫Credevo che avrebbe purificato le persone dalle impurità."

#: search2:search2_4293C089_1C85_48B3_A4BD_6329F82D9EC6
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 769acfe2a797fc661bbba4656ed1e730710e63db9d47a7b0960bfaa644e698f6
#. default-sha256: d7a4ae49e74e765fefc6d4c7326e94adb4021fd5f1099bd71ff1749673925b2d
msgctxt "search2:search2_4293C089_1C85_48B3_A4BD_6329F82D9EC6"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫But if you would give me a chance, I would like to explain myself. ⟪k:2⟫I was but a "
"young girl at the time. ⟪k:3⟫And to a child, her mother is the world. ⟪k:4⟫Anything she says is "
"the absolute truth.⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫So when my mother’s claims so happened to coincide with a lucky "
"miracle, my young mind was set in stone.⟪k:8⟫⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫I was a saint.⟪k:12⟫⟪k:13⟫⟪k:14⟫My "
"blood could heal the sick.⟪k:15⟫⟪k:16⟫⟪k:17⟫And nothing would convince me otherwise.⟪k:18⟫⟪k:19⟫"
"⟪k:20⟫⟪k:21⟫After all, I was but a girl of six years old."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Vorrei che tu mi dessi l’opportunità di darti una spiegazione.⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫Ero solo una "
"bambina a quei tempi. ⟪k:4⟫E per una bambina, la madre è il suo mondo. ⟪k:5⟫Qualunque cosa lei "
"dica è verità assoluta.⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫⟪k:8⟫E così, quando le affermazioni di mia madre coincisero con "
"un miracolo inatteso, la mia giovane mente si convinse all’istante.⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫Ero una "
"santa.⟪k:13⟫⟪k:14⟫⟪k:15⟫Il mio sangue poteva curare i malati.⟪k:16⟫⟪k:17⟫⟪k:18⟫E nulla avrebbe "
"potuto farmi cambiare idea.⟪k:19⟫⟪k:20⟫⟪k:21⟫⟪k:22⟫Dopotutto, ero soltanto una bambina di sei "
"anni."

#: search2:search2_74DF6E1C_9F3F_4A02_88FC_8F0F637CAEDB
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 7e3917d55143815aa1b711d186e8613a28886549615603350e545a21e0b7d9af
#. default-sha256: a9eab23d91e5b0541a71ae07254eb7b04e5798c2ed02288cb1ba646dd38d8efa
msgctxt "search2:search2_74DF6E1C_9F3F_4A02_88FC_8F0F637CAEDB"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫It didn’t take long for word of the miracle-performing child of God to spread. ⟪k:2⟫"
"Travelers from faraway lands came to our village, all in search of aid.⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫Driven by a "
"mixture of elation and duty, I gave my blessings unto every pilgrim who sought them. ⟪k:6⟫I gave "
"them my blood, yes.⟪k:7⟫⟪k:8⟫⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫My young hands were perpetually covered in wounds. ⟪k:11⟫"
"Running out of skin on my fingers, I cut the back of my hands, my palms, my wrists. ⟪k:12⟫Before "
"long, they had turned into swollen, carved-up, black-and-red horrors, ⟪k:13⟫and so I kept them "
"wrapped in cloth at all times. ⟪k:14⟫The only time I uncovered them was to give blood to those "
"who sought it.⟪k:15⟫⟪k:16⟫⟪k:17⟫My lacerated hands were, in no uncertain terms, gruesome and "
"unsightly, ⟪k:18⟫but the believers who came to see me all wept at my “selfless sacrifice.”⟪k:19⟫"
"⟪k:20⟫⟪k:21⟫⟪k:22⟫And so I came to cherish those wounds."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Non ci volle molto perché le voci sulla bambina prodigio figlia di Dio si spargessero. "
"⟪k:2⟫Viaggiatori provenienti da terre remote vennero al nostro villaggio in cerca di aiuto.⟪k:3⟫ "
"E così, spinta da un misto di responsabilità ed entusiasmo, diedi la mia benedizione ad ogni "
"pellegrino che la desiderasse. ⟪k:4⟫Sì, diedi loro il mio sangue.⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫⟪k:8⟫Le mie "
"giovani mani erano perennemente ricoperte di ferite. ⟪k:9⟫Rimanendo a corto di pelle sulle dita, "
"mi tagliavo il dorso delle mani,⟪k:10⟫i palmi, i polsi. ⟪k:11⟫In poco tempo, le mie mani si "
"trasformarono in orrori sfigurati, rossi e gonfi, ⟪k:12⟫perciò le tenevo coperte sotto i vestiti "
"per tutto il tempo. ⟪k:13⟫Le uniche volte in cui le scoprivo era quando qualcuno chiedeva il mio "
"sangue.⟪k:14⟫⟪k:15⟫⟪k:16⟫Le mie mani lacerate erano—⟪k:17⟫⟪k:18⟫detto molto francamente—⟪k:19⟫"
"⟪k:20⟫orrende e raccapriccianti, ⟪k:21⟫ma i credenti che venivano a trovarmi ⟪k:22⟫"
"piangevano⟪k:23⟫ dinanzi al mio “generoso sacrificio”.⟪k:24⟫⟪k:25⟫⟪k:26⟫⟪k:27⟫Giunsi così ad "
"onorare quelle ferite."

#: search2:search2_B6BD1699_7737_4379_B796_F6F4888EB0FD
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 6e0abd817ba5d06a37faffada255b6f35697bc47b38b1c7df3727fd9f8282dad
#. default-sha256: e8bc5cd1f89782174bb21255b8414394061bfe1ab6faa884776612078b25fd0c
msgctxt "search2:search2_B6BD1699_7737_4379_B796_F6F4888EB0FD"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫But the next day, ⟪k:2⟫I was sold off.⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫Men I had never seen before "
"carried me by the arms and tossed me into a carriage. ⟪k:6⟫Confused and panicked, I stuck my head "
"out, searching for my mother.⟪k:7⟫⟪k:8⟫⟪k:9⟫Off in the shadow of the house, ⟪k:10⟫I saw her with "
"a strange man—⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫⟪k:13⟫⟪k:14⟫accepting a bag of coins."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Ma il giorno dopo, ⟪k:2⟫fui venduta.⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫Uomini che non avevo mai visto prima "
"mi presero per le braccia⟪k:6⟫e mi gettarono in un carro. ⟪k:7⟫Confusa ed impaurita, mi affacciai "
"fuori,⟪k:8⟫cercando mia madre con lo sguardo.⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫La vidi all’ombra di casa nostra, "
"⟪k:12⟫insieme ad uno sconosciuto—⟪k:13⟫⟪k:14⟫⟪k:15⟫⟪k:16⟫mentre riceveva una borsa piena di "
"monete."

#: search2:search2_E6FB4A24_7FE8_4101_A9C9_F5A1C933E065
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: cb06fe6e5a542d65103d269d804044efdd554671d4d9b8d47e79e28bfdbc901f
#. default-sha256: 24473d08d9d5044b9bb1f5e895ed0cf7bc177b5b5674ebae81bb682b8dce2404
msgctxt "search2:search2_E6FB4A24_7FE8_4101_A9C9_F5A1C933E065"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫The carriage rocked back and forth, back and forth as it rolled along a dirt road. ⟪k:2⟫"
"Shaking and bouncing within it, I struggled with overwhelming grief and despair. ⟪k:3⟫It was, "
"perhaps, the first time in my life I had felt such a powerful emotion.⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫I didn’t "
"know ⟪k:7⟫what⟪k:8⟫ I felt so much despair over, though. ⟪k:9⟫Obviously, it was over my present "
"predicament, but I wasn’t sure what about it hurt the most.⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫⟪k:13⟫Was it that I "
"had been pawned off like a slave? ⟪k:14⟫Was it that my mother—the mother of a saint—had been "
"blinded by money? ⟪k:15⟫Was it that the villagers had watched in silence as a disciple of the "
"Lord was thrown into a carriage?⟪k:16⟫⟪k:17⟫⟪k:18⟫⟪k:19⟫Or was it that I, daughter of God, ⟪k:20⟫"
"lamented my misfortune like a mortal?"
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Il carro dondolava avanti e indietro, avanti e indietro, mentre marciava lungo una "
"strada sterrata. ⟪k:2⟫Barcollando e sobbalzando al suo interno, dovetti sopportare un dolore e "
"una tristezza immensi.⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫Fu la prima volta in vita mia in cui provai un’emozione così "
"forte.⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫Tuttavia, non sapevo per ⟪k:8⟫cosa⟪k:9⟫ provassi tanta disperazione. ⟪k:10⟫"
"Ovviamente, era per la situazione in cui mi trovavo, ma non sapevo bene cosa mi facesse male più "
"di tutto.⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫⟪k:13⟫⟪k:14⟫Era l’essere stata venduta come una schiava? ⟪k:15⟫Era il fatto "
"che mia madre—⟪k:16⟫⟪k:17⟫la madre di una santa—⟪k:18⟫⟪k:19⟫fosse stata accecata dal denaro?⟪k:20⟫"
"⟪k:21⟫Che gli abitanti del villaggio fossero rimasti a guardare in silenzio, mentre un discepolo "
"del Signore veniva gettato in un carro?⟪k:22⟫⟪k:23⟫⟪k:24⟫⟪k:25⟫O era il fatto che io, figlia di "
"Dio, ⟪k:26⟫mi dispiacessi per la mia sciagura come una mortale?"

#: search2:search2_FF2F5CD2_17B0_44F3_8CA1_E7DA2DDDB0FE
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 4b2c74f70f64a15aa1c96a3471c09af5022bc24c54b1735f327b6501f2545b3c
#. default-sha256: 256a9c35d789f73f851c24d59c3186cad074a9e07d226bd04ddd43c9ae016607
msgctxt "search2:search2_FF2F5CD2_17B0_44F3_8CA1_E7DA2DDDB0FE"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫The third week, the carriage arrived at a city. ⟪k:1⟫It was much larger than the village I "
"had grown up in, with many, many more people crowding the streets. ⟪k:2⟫Something about them ⟪k:3⟫"
"felt⟪k:4⟫ different too.⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫They all spoke in a tongue foreign to me, ⟪k:8⟫which is "
"when I realized I was far, far away from home."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫La terza settimana, il carrò arrivò in una città. ⟪k:1⟫Era decisamente⟪k:2⟫più grande del "
"villaggio dove ero cresciuta, con molte più persone⟪k:3⟫ad affollare le strade. ⟪k:4⟫Oltretutto, "
"percepivo in loro qualcosa di diverso.⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫Parlavano tutti una lingua per me "
"sconosciuta, ⟪k:8⟫fu allora che capii⟪k:9⟫che mi trovavo molto, molto lontano da casa."

#: search2:search2_DC4CD8EC_3727_4CDB_B254_F3D9D4B750B2
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 6c15ddb8981abd24ed9e76faf96ad9f617d3c8902cbc3e84bd9748fde2c94bb1
#. default-sha256: 92cd5f36fed723973c0fcc7ec6e3ce200b48fd4ba0fe00d9a53dbb831916731b
msgctxt "search2:search2_DC4CD8EC_3727_4CDB_B254_F3D9D4B750B2"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫I was delivered to the lavishly decorated mansion of the region’s lord. ⟪k:2⟫Brightly "
"colored flowers bloomed wildly in the garden as guests laughed and ate extravagant meals.⟪k:3⟫"
"⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫And in addition to them, there were probably four times as many slaves moving about the "
"grounds.⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫⟪k:8⟫Getting a range of looks from everyone we passed—from smartly dressed men "
"to scrawny, emaciated servants—I was led to the lord’s chambers.⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫The lord "
"was surrounded by beautiful women. ⟪k:13⟫Perhaps they were slaves, or perhaps they were "
"prostitutes—I couldn’t tell. ⟪k:14⟫Among them were some girls hardly older than me. ⟪k:15⟫They "
"all wore thin swathes of cloth, barely covering themselves at all.⟪k:16⟫⟪k:17⟫⟪k:18⟫⟪k:19⟫The "
"lord looked me up and down, and with a laugh, he said,"
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Mi consegnarono alla sontuosa villa del lord del posto. ⟪k:2⟫Fiori dai colori vivaci "
"sbocciavano senza sosta nel giardino, mentre gli ospiti ridevano e mangiavano pasti stravaganti."
"⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫E oltre a loro, c’erano probabilmente il quadruplo di schiavi che facevano avanti "
"e indietro.⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫⟪k:8⟫Attiravo gli sguardi di tutti coloro che incontravamo—⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫da "
"uomini elegantemente rivestiti a servitori magri e scheletrici—⟪k:11⟫⟪k:12⟫mentre venivo condotta "
"alla stanza del lord.⟪k:13⟫⟪k:14⟫⟪k:15⟫⟪k:16⟫Il padrone della reggia era circondato da donne "
"bellissime.⟪k:17⟫⟪k:18⟫Forse erano schiave, o forse erano prostitute—⟪k:19⟫⟪k:20⟫non avrei saputo "
"dirlo. ⟪k:21⟫Tra loro c’erano alcune ragazze poco più grandi di me. ⟪k:22⟫Indossavano tutte vesti "
"sottili, che le coprivano a malapena.⟪k:23⟫⟪k:24⟫⟪k:25⟫⟪k:26⟫Il lord mi squadrò dalla testa ai "
"piedi, e con una risata disse:"

#: search2:search2_C36F63C9_F725_4400_A3C1_2F80C9ED50DF
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 148d6c89e95865efbc6bc7c7d1fc25e4cdcbd590ff72945b79d077306844b825
#. default-sha256: 28347913bb60935a279c617a146cb4ca37f3d68cfddc2ec801939fb32e7e73c6
msgctxt "search2:search2_C36F63C9_F725_4400_A3C1_2F80C9ED50DF"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫So the lord forced his will upon me.⟪k:1⟫⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫He bound my hands and feet and cut me "
"without my permission, filling a goblet with my blood and passing it around to his guests."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫E così il lord impose il suo volere su di me.⟪k:1⟫⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫Mi legò mani e piedi e mi tagliò "
"senza il mio permesso, riempendo una coppa col mio sangue e facendola girare tra i suoi ospiti."

#: search2:search2_77C89967_DD3E_4BBB_BCE1_E8B26CF824F5
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 21537ed293929f81e171b7252a464254c4ec4aa8ee010d4e937a4945fa25de22
#. default-sha256: d32594a01dc13fa11fdb684a11d38613d3d0b788d11a65630c34417fd7c6ba77
msgctxt "search2:search2_77C89967_DD3E_4BBB_BCE1_E8B26CF824F5"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Every time he threw a banquet, he drained me of my blood.⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫It became nearly "
"impossible to find a spot on either of my arms that ⟪k:4⟫wasn’t⟪k:5⟫ a swollen, reddish-black "
"gash. ⟪k:6⟫And soon, because my arms weren’t providing enough blood for him, the cutting spread "
"to my legs.⟪k:7⟫⟪k:8⟫⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫I lived in a haze of half-consciousness. ⟪k:11⟫Honestly, I’m "
"amazed it didn’t kill me, though perhaps the lord was simply taking care not to take more than my "
"body could spare.⟪k:12⟫⟪k:13⟫⟪k:14⟫⟪k:15⟫Watching the wealthy partygoers laugh and sip my blood "
"through bleary eyes, another wave of despair came over me. ⟪k:16⟫My miracles—my blood—were not "
"meant to be an appetizer at a feast. They were meant for the sick and the poor.⟪k:17⟫⟪k:18⟫⟪k:19⟫"
"But despite my wishes, the lord persisted to squeeze me dry day in and day out for his own "
"enjoyment."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Ogni volta che organizzava un banchetto, mi privava del mio sangue.⟪k:2⟫ Divenne quasi "
"impossibile trovare altri punti sulle mie braccia⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫senza⟪k:5⟫ tagli gonfi e rossastri. "
"⟪k:6⟫E presto, non riuscendo più a procurarsi abbastanza sangue dalle mie braccia, iniziò a "
"concentrarsi sulle gambe.⟪k:7⟫⟪k:8⟫⟪k:9⟫Vivevo in uno stato di semicoscienza. ⟪k:10⟫Ad essere "
"onesta, sono sorpresa che ciò non mi avesse uccisa, anche se forse il lord si stava semplicemente "
"assicurando di non prendere ⟪k:11⟫più sangue⟪k:12⟫ di quanto il mio corpo potesse produrre.⟪k:13⟫"
"⟪k:14⟫⟪k:15⟫⟪k:16⟫⟪k:17⟫Osservando i ricchi partecipanti alla festa ridere e sorseggiare il mio "
"sangue attraverso i miei occhi annebbiati, fui investita da un’altra ondata di disperazione. "
"⟪k:18⟫I miei miracoli—⟪k:19⟫⟪k:20⟫il mio sangue—⟪k:21⟫⟪k:22⟫non erano destinati a fare da "
"aperitivo alle feste. Erano destinati ai poveri e ai malati.⟪k:23⟫⟪k:24⟫⟪k:25⟫Ma nonostante le "
"mie volontà, il lord continuò a spremermi giorno dopo giorno per il suo stesso divertimento."

#: search2:search2_265BA5DF_1814_4DFB_94E0_36DEC30575C5
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: ba101e763db109b0e633ec93caa7e246e87d16e0a48a580b573c354459463fbb
#. default-sha256: df49650a1a1642d5efc2092aa37b2cac61301b14bad96ddd37a847c2a371ecf0
msgctxt "search2:search2_265BA5DF_1814_4DFB_94E0_36DEC30575C5"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫Suddenly, I found myself released from my bonds. ⟪k:1⟫But my body had grown so weak from "
"being tied up for so long, I didn’t have the strength to hold myself up—and so I collapsed to the "
"floor.⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫I was still trying to figure out what was happening when the lord drew "
"a sword, raising it high above his head. ⟪k:6⟫His words in that moment reached me with perfect "
"clarity:"
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫D’un tratto, mi ritrovai libera dalle catene. ⟪k:1⟫Ma ero diventata talmente debole per "
"essere rimasta incatenata così a lungo da non avere la forza di tenermi su, e così collassai a "
"terra.⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫⟪k:5⟫Stavo ancora cercando di capire cosa stesse accadendo, quando il lord "
"sguainò la spada, sollevandola oltre la sua testa. ⟪k:6⟫In quel momento, le sue parole mi "
"giunsero con estrema chiarezza:"

#: search2:search2_836438AF_6ED4_4876_982D_86366DA1A3A5
#. Edit msgstr; keep protected ⟪k:N⟫ markers in source order.
#. native-sha256: 673981a4927f0bd1a59f0f0d0869651224292410e0428dd7558db744a3acc217
#. default-sha256: 036b81e6f81f9260d521906bb96d5a686f3aec6ca0b2b1e45f0ebc54d3e8e673
msgctxt "search2:search2_836438AF_6ED4_4876_982D_86366DA1A3A5"
msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫A witch?⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫Why was he calling me a witch?⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫I was the holy "
"daughter of God; ⟪k:8⟫I had certainly never made a pact with the Devil.⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫What "
"could have given him that idea? What was in store for me now? Had God performed some kind of "
"miracle for him? ⟪k:12⟫Dozens of thoughts and questions floated through my mind as death hung "
"over me.⟪k:13⟫⟪k:14⟫⟪k:15⟫⟪k:16⟫I couldn’t comprehend anything, and so I didn’t feel any fear or "
"anger at my impending death. ⟪k:17⟫I was simply curious:⟪k:18⟫⟪k:19⟫⟪k:20⟫What had happened to me?"
"⟪k:21⟫⟪k:22⟫⟪k:23⟫But before I had a chance to find that answer—⟪k:24⟫⟪k:25⟫⟪k:26⟫⟪k:27⟫the lord "
"swung down his blade."
msgstr ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫Una strega?⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫⟪k:4⟫Perché mi chiamava “strega”?⟪k:5⟫⟪k:6⟫⟪k:7⟫Ero la santa "
"figlia di Dio; ⟪k:8⟫di certo non avevo mai stretto un patto col Diavolo.⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫Chi "
"poteva avergli dato quell’idea? ⟪k:12⟫Cosa c’era in serbo per me?⟪k:13⟫⟪k:14⟫Dio gli aveva forse "
"concesso un qualche tipo di miracolo? ⟪k:15⟫La mia mente venne attraversata da numerosi pensieri "
"e altrettante domande, mentre la morte incombeva su di me.⟪k:16⟫⟪k:17⟫⟪k:18⟫⟪k:19⟫Non riuscivo a "
"capire nulla, perciò non provai né paura né rabbia per la mia morte imminente. ⟪k:20⟫Ero "
"semplicemente curiosa:⟪k:21⟫⟪k:22⟫⟪k:23⟫Cosa mi era successo?⟪k:24⟫⟪k:25⟫⟪k:26⟫Ma prima che "
"riuscissi ad avere la possibilità di trovare una risposta—⟪k:27⟫⟪k:28⟫⟪k:29⟫⟪k:30⟫il lord sferrò "
"un fendente con la sua lama."

#: search2:search2_E9D2BF9F_A6F9_4B5D_8A29_428A3E90DD8C
